  "notes": [
    "Chaos run: The first worker reads requests and never answers (a hung process); its /stats keeps answering, so the agent says READY and only the gateway's own header timeout (lowered to 2 s) can detect it.",
    "What this embedded mock cluster cannot show here: A frozen process stops its heartbeat too, which the registry notices after the suspect threshold (10 s here); the mock keeps answering /stats so that the breaker is the only detector. SIGSTOP of a real worker is the process-level version (not run).",
    "Windows follow when the fault was really applied and cleared. Gateway counters (attempts per request, retries) are read at the tick that opens and closes a window (every 1s), so an attempt of a request in flight at a boundary falls in the next window; the per-request figures come from the clients.",
    "Closed-loop clients: 14 for the whole run on 32 request slots (24 left serving). Closed-loop clients wait for each response, so a failing worker also slows the offered load.",
    "Load average (1, 5 and 15 minutes) at the start of the run: 2.69 3.67 4.15; at the end: 3.18 3.64 4.11."
  ],
